# Outside el (§5.2), inside el++ (§5.4). Under el the axiom is ENUMERATED as
# omitted, so the verdict is INCONCLUSIVE (exit 2), never coherent; under el++ it
# is decided.
#
# ObjectHasSelf: in the OWL 2 EL profile, outside el's ELH⊥R+ (a case where
# 'we do EL' would overclaim for el), and in el++ on a simple role.

@prefix :     <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix swrl: <http://www.w3.org/2003/11/swrl#> .

<http://example.org/t> a owl:Ontology .
:A a owl:Class . :r a owl:ObjectProperty .
:A rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty :r ; owl:hasSelf true ] .
